 "FOSFORILASA B:Fosforilasa b is the inactive form of glucógeno fosforilasa, which must be activated to participate in glycogen breakdown.", "UDP-GLUCOSA:UDP-glucosa is a nucleotide sugar that plays a crucial role in metabolism, particularly in the metabolism of galactose. It is essential for the synthesis of glycogen and other macromolecules, functioning as a glucose donor in these biochemical processes.", "UDP-GLUCOSA PIROFOSFORIILASA:UDP-glucosa pirofosforilasa is an enzyme that catalyzes the formation of UDP-glucose from glucose-1-phosphate and UTP.", "FOSFOGLUCOMUTASA:Fosfoglucomutasa is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in carbohydrate metabolism by catalyzing the conversion of glucosa-1-fosfato (glucose-1-phosphate) to glucosa-6-fosfato (glucose-6-phosphate). This conversion is essential for facilitating the entry of glucose into various metabolic pathways, thereby contributing to the overall regulation of glucose metabolism.", "TORRENTE SANGUÍNEO:Torrente sanguíneo refers to the bloodstream, the circulatory system that transports glucose and other nutrients throughout the body.", "GLUCOGENÓLISIS:Gluconeogenesis is the metabolic pathway that results in the generation of glucose from non-carbohydrate substrates, primarily occurring in the liver.", "GLUCOGENOGÉNESIS:Glycogenesis is the process of synthesizing glycogen from glucose, primarily occurring in the liver and muscle tissues.", "FOSFORILASA KINASA:", "GLYCOGEN STORAGE DISEASE TYPE I:Glycogen Storage Disease Type I (GSDI) is a genetic disorder characterized by the accumulation of glycogen in the liver and kidneys due to enzyme deficiencies.", "HEPATOMEGALY:Hepatomegaly is a clinical condition characterized by the mild enlargement of the liver. It is commonly associated with various metabolic disorders, particularly glycogen storage diseases such as type I glucogenosis (GSDI) and type VI glucogenosis (GSDVI). This condition can also occur in patients with fructose-1,6-bisphosphate deficiency, where fatty acid accumulation contributes to liver enlargement. Additionally, hepatomegaly may be observed in individuals with Wilson's disease, further highlighting its association with a range of hepatic and metabolic disorders. Overall, hepatomegaly serves as an important clinical manifestation indicative of underlying liver-related issues.", "GLUCOSE-6-PHOSPHATASE:Glucose-6-phosphatase is an enzyme critical for glucose metabolism, deficiency of which leads to GSDI.", "GLUCOSE-6-PHOSPHATE TRANSPORTER:Glucose-6-phosphate transporter is an enzyme involved in the transport of glucose-6-phosphate within cells, deficiency of which is associated with GSDI.", "VON GIERKE DISEASE:Von Gierke disease is another name for Glycogen Storage Disease Type I, specifically related to glucose-6-phosphatase deficiency."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}